# ── Local secrets & operator config — NEVER commit (see CLAUDE.md) ──
.env
.env.*
# Templates are safe to track (no leading slash: applies at every depth,
# e.g. .env.example, deploy/.env.example) — they document non-secret
# defaults, never real values. Re-ignore patterns below: *.token, *.vault,
# secrets*.json/yml, *.local.json/yml (never match ".example", so this
# negation can't reopen them) and vault-pass* (deliberate exception: it
# DOES still shadow vault-pass.example, because a vault-pass file's whole
# content is the password — there is no non-secret default to template).
# It cannot reach inside a fully-ignored directory (/deploy/config/, dev/local/)
# — that is a known git limitation, not a gap in this pattern.
# ORDERING IS LOAD-BEARING: any secret pattern added ABOVE !*.example is
# punched through by it. New secret patterns go BELOW this line.
!*.example
*.token
*.vault
vault-pass*
secrets*.json
secrets*.yml
# Issue #844/#845: the epic's (#841) persistent local-state location for
# file-backed secrets (deploy/config/secrets/) and operator TLS
# (deploy/config/tls/). Anchored (leading slash) for the same reason #254
# anchored the old root-level config/ rule: so this ignores the one
# directory under deploy/ and never something coincidentally named config/
# elsewhere in the tree (e.g. frontend/src/screens/config/). Issue #845 removed the legacy
# repo-root /config/ convention this superseded -- compose.yaml no longer
# references anything under ../config/ (relative to deploy/), only
# ./config/ (this entry). No compatibility migration needed (epic #841).
/deploy/config/
# Issue #845: Compose auto-loads this file alongside compose.yaml when
# present (see compose.override.example.yaml, which IS committed and safe
# to track -- it carries no secrets, only the development topology).
/deploy/compose.override.yaml
# Issue #845: reserved for any future generated/derived local state under
# deploy/ (e.g. a future generator script's scratch output, #847) that
# isn't operator-authored config and doesn't belong in deploy/config/.
# Nothing writes here yet.
/deploy/.generated/
dev/local/
*.local.json
*.local.yml
# Issue #957: untracked local-docs convention — any *.local.md holds
# machine/lab-specific instructions (docs/testing.md describes the
# convention; docs/testing.local.md is the live-testing entry point).
*.local.md
# Issue #28: deploy/scripts/keycloak-realm-import.sh's scratch copy of a
# realm export with a REAL client secret substituted in (never the
# committed deploy/keycloak/realm/waypoint-realm.json placeholder) -- see
# that script's header comment for why it lives under deploy/ rather than
# /tmp. Anchored: only the one script-owned directory, not a generic name.
/deploy/.keycloak-import-scratch/

# Certificates & keys
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
# Issue #844 renamed the dev nginx pair from dev-cert.pem/dev-key.pem to the
# generic tls.crt/tls.key names deploy/nginx/conf.d/default.conf now uses (so
# one config serves either the dev-generated pair or an operator's real
# certs). `tls.key` is still covered by *.key above, but nothing above
# matches a .crt -- and a bare `*.crt` would be too broad for a repo that may
# one day carry a legitimately-committed trust anchor (e.g. a test CA
# fixture). Anchored to the single generated location instead:
# deploy/nginx/certs/generate-dev-certs.sh's output, and nothing else.
# Operator TLS at deploy/config/tls/ is already covered by /deploy/config/.
/deploy/nginx/certs/tls.crt

# Build output
# Audited #362 (follow-up to #254, which anchored config/ -> /config/ after
# it swallowed frontend/src/screens/config/ as app source): every pattern
# below is intentionally LEFT unanchored. Each is a build-tool-owned
# directory name (.NET bin/obj, npm node_modules/dist, pytest/dotnet-test
# TestResults, CPython __pycache__) that legitimately recurs at every
# nesting depth (e.g. backend/*/bin/, frontend/vite-plugins/dist/) and,
# unlike "config", is never a plausible name for a hand-written source
# directory - confirmed by `find` across backend/ and frontend/src/ turning
# up no such collisions. Anchoring any of these to root would MISS the
# nested build output they exist to ignore. Do not anchor without re-
# confirming a real collision first.
bin/
obj/
TestResults/
# Pester's default NUnit output (Invoke-Pester -CI), written at the cwd of
# whatever ran it -- issue #1099's WaypointScan.ShapeInventory.Tests.ps1 etc.
testResults.xml
node_modules/
dist/
frontend/build/
# Python bytecode from the sanitize scanner and its test suite
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor/OS noise
.vscode/
.instructions/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
